  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 953 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nThe aforementioned frontal boundary should be to our south by\nFriday night into early Saturday, allowing mostly dry conditions\nto take over the area. However, as sfc high pressure resides over\nthe Appalachians and the boundary stalls to our south, continued\nlow chances for shower/thunderstorm development will exist in the\neastern zones of our CWA through the weekend. This is low\nconfidence due to model uncertainty in the exact evolution of the\nfrontal boundary as it shifts south of the area, however, trends\nhave continued to stall it before gradually lifting it slightly\nback northeastward through the latter part of the weekend. Have\ncontinued with blended guidance for now. Otherwise, high\ntemperatures are forecast to reach the low to mid 90s with heat\nindices up to around 100 degrees as an upper level ridge continues\nto influence the region from the west. If you have outdoor plans,\nbe sure to seek shade and stay hydrated to avoid heat illness.",
